{#
insight/_external_link.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The link out to wherever an insight's payload url points.

Accepts:
  url    string
  kind   InsightKind
  class  optional extra classes for the anchor

Shared by the radar card, the pane strip and the reading-pane strip, which had
three copies of it — every one of them printing GitHub's octocat and the word
"GitHub" for any payload url at all.

That held only because GitHub is the one extractor setting `url` today. The
same assumption already cost the undated section its name: it was called "From
your repos" because repos were all that ever reached it, right up until a
parcel with no stated ETA did. A mark that says which service a link belongs to
has to be chosen from the KIND, not from the fact that nothing else has needed
one yet.

The host is the fallback, and it is deliberately modest: it names where the
link goes without claiming to know what is there.
#}
<a href="{{ url }}"
   target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
   data-insight-open-url
   class="inline-flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-line px-2.5 py-1
          text-xs font-medium text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink transition-colors {{ class|default('') }}">
    {% if kind.value starts with 'github-' %}
        {# The brand's own name rather than a catalogue key — "GitHub" is not a
           word any locale translates. #}
        <i class="fa-brands fa-github text-[11px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        GitHub
    {% else %}
        {# Host only: `url|split('/')` puts it at index 2 for every absolute
           http(s) URL, and an extractor that produced anything else falls back
           to printing the url itself rather than a slice of nonsense. #}
        <i class="fa-solid fa-link text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        {{ url|split('/')|slice(2, 1)|first|default(url) }}
    {% endif %}
    <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-up-right-from-square text-[9px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
</a>
